<p>I like the idea, but I too am bugged by the resources being thrown into a relatively easily contained SCP.</p>
<p>Reading through the article, it seems that only Red instances would cause a problem for the foundation. The other illusions could be easily contained by simply keeping 1410 in a decent sized room with D-Class actors posted as &quot;guards&quot;.</p>
<p>The foundation could use the time previously spent keeping 1410 happy researching how to limit the more troublesome illusions.</p>
<p>I really like the idea otherwise, and I think I could be convinced if there were just a little stronger justification - for example, observers beginning to succumb to the same delusions as 1410, or the illusions gradually becoming corporeal.</p>

